<title>ITALY: Italy declines comment on lira ERM re-entry.</title>
<headline>Italy declines comment on lira ERM re-entry.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian government sources said the government would neither confirm or deny a report that the European Union's monetary committee would meet at the weekend to discuss the lira's re-entry to the EU exchange rate mechanism.</p>
<p>A senior source on the sidelines of the European Banking Congress in Frankfurt told Reuters that Italy had requested a meeting of the monetary committee for Saturday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are not saying anything on this matter,&quot; one Italian government source said. Earlier Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi said Italy would ask for a return to the ERM by the end of November.   -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
